    "official_contract": "Current official Sandbox guide Named Sandboxes requires a deployed App for named Sandboxes. Pinned SDK cli/utils.py 163-201 explicitly normalizes display headers into snake_case JSON keys. Receipts/short quotes are retained in the failure reports; external full text is outside Git.",
    "official_runtime_contract": "Pinned modal/types.py SandboxRuntime at line 59 and sandbox.py _validate_sandbox_runtime at 166-170 were read. Official Sandboxes guide Runtimes explicitly allows omission/provider choice and restricts GPU Sandboxes to gvisor. Full external receipts and short quotes are in failure-analysis-v3."
  },
  "closed_material_findings": [
    {
      "id": "named_ephemeral_contract",
      "status": "closed",
      "evidence": "The ephemeral probe no longer supplies Sandbox.name, and identifiers no longer invent a Sandbox name. Recovery uses exact owned App ID plus atomic round/attempt tags. The real pinned protobuf request probe asserts name is empty and absent from ListFields; it does not introduce a deployed/long-lived App."
    },
    {
      "id": "actual_cli_json_contract",
      "status": "closed",
      "evidence": "preflight.stopped_app, runtime exact App matching and official stop polling all consume app_id/description/state/tasks. The independent real SDK display_table renderer produces those keys, and the full new SDK/runner probe passes rendered rows through read_stopped_apps and reconcile_stop. The native recovery inventory reclassifies to no active Apps under the corrected helper."
    },
    {
      "id": "redaction_before_truncation",
      "status": "closed",
      "evidence": "A definite reviewer finding showed truncation-before-redaction could leak a token prefix crossing byte/character position 4000. Author moved replacement to the complete message, sorts three actual environment token values longest-first, then truncates to 4000 characters. A boundary/overlap regression and a real-SDK INVALID_ARGUMENT fake-transport case pass without exposed fake credential fragments. The reviewer did not read or output actual credentials."
    },
    {
      "id": "new_source_closure",
      "status": "closed",
      "evidence": "AUDIT_PATH points to this v2 audit, SOURCE_FILES has all 13 files including inspection/reconciliation/fixture/tests, and checked_sources requires the exact complete file set, independent author/reviewer roles, every source and audit to equal selected committed bytes, and hash agreement. Independent probes reject the historical nine-file audit, self-authoring, missing scope, hash drift, dirty source and symlinks."
    },
    {
      "id": "one_off_first_failure",
      "status": "closed_in_separate_audit",
      "evidence": "execution-probe-reconciliation-audit-v1.json independently accepts only the fixed original attempt/receipt/revision/reservation. Exact official STOPPED lifecycle and complete finished-inclusive empty history, full original Git blob reconstruction, before/after validate_state and single-CAS/rejected-CAS probes were verified. This rule preserves the complete original failed receipt and USD0.40; it does not generalize InvalidError or empty active lists."
    },
    {
      "id": "unsupported_runtime_override",
      "status": "closed",
      "evidence": "The final pre-issuance contract check found pinned SandboxRuntime only permits gvisor/vm and the official GPU Sandbox guide requires gvisor. Author omitted the unsupported explicit runc field. The real pinned validator rejects runc, default None serializes like omitted runtime, and the final real-SDK request probe requires runtime absent from ListFields as well as name absent. The final source hashes above bind this correction; no audit authorizes the former runc override."
    }
  ],
  "earlier_core_controls_rechecked": [
    "One L4 Sandbox, existing Image ID im-1b8GW96gjEVRiK1vg5Jqa0, 2 CPU request=limit, 8192 MiB request=limit, server timeout_secs=600, blocked network and no snapshots, Secrets, Volumes or image build.",
    "Fresh official billing/rates and inventory precede a successful durable full USD0.40 reservation CAS. Missing/higher/nonfinite/negative rates block; the actual paid boundary rechecks freshness. No paid create occurs on failed CAS.",
    "Exactly one direct SandboxCreate with retry=None and timeout=180. The whole raw coroutine runs on the SDK synchronizer loop; task-ID scheduling shares the remaining monotonic create budget. The high-level SDK loader and its cancellation shield are absent.",
    "A hard 120-second cleanup budget covers owned-ID stop/poll, App context exit, client close and remaining-time official App-list polling. hard_wait does not wait past the deadline for cancelled shield cleanup; failures remain unresolved.",
    "Lost response with a recovered exact owned Sandbox ID is explicitly terminated and observed terminal; lost response with no recovered ID remains unresolved. A new generic INVALID_ARGUMENT case with no ID also remains unresolved; the special first-failure rule is separate.",
    "Financial policy, durable origin, exact legacy USD4.73 carry, retained official gross high-water and all additive new bounds remain unchanged. No automatically released reservation or paid retry is introduced.",
    "P1 .github/workflows/omni-revision.yml remains client-only. New workflow operations have distinct if branches; inspection creates no compute and reconciliation creates no compute or AppStop. The new paid source gate and old unresolved-status guard remain fail-closed until required audit/commit/state conditions are satisfied."
  ],
